PHASE 1: PERCUSSIVE SKELETON

Distorted 808 kick: scalpel-sharp transient, phase-locked sub-weight strictly 35–50 Hz, tight punchy decay that punches through without bloom.

Dry metallic snare/clap hybrid: crisp high-frequency snap + white-noise burst, absolute zero reverb tail.

Groove: minimalist half-time trap feel with subtle, purposeful syncopation and restrained swing — maximum breathing room between hits.

▉ ▊ ▋ ▌ ✧ ▌ ▋ ▊ ▉

PHASE 2: THE BASS LEAD (FILTHY WOBBLE & GROWL)

Multi-oscillator FM synthesis bass: layered sines + gritty modulators creating rubbery-metallic yet filthy, slithering timbre. Heavy modulated resonant filter (low-pass/band-pass) for organic wobble and evolving movement. Expressive downward pitch envelopes + subtle MPE-style bends on every note.

Processing: crushed into aggressive brick via brutal OTT-style multiband compression; light saturation/distortion for added filth and harmonics without mud.

Rhythm: sparse, impactful note placement — each sound evolves internally through modulation rather than rapid gating. Let the wobble and filter movement carry the aggression.

▉ ▊ ▋ ▌ ✧ ▌ ▋ ▊ ▉

PHASE 3: THE SPATIAL VOID

Core signals mono-locked and dead-center.

Off-beat only: ultra-sparse randomized panned micro-foley (hydraulic hiss, glass shatter, guttural breath/grunt).

Master sidechain triggered by the kick: total annihilation of everything (including noise floor) into vast, engineered silence — the voids must feel heavier than the drops.

Deliver cold, clinical, high-impact minimalism. Textural brutality through subtraction. Maximum psychoacoustic weight via sub mass and silence. Raw, uncompromised, anti-mainstream filth.
